  "question": {
    "text": "One mole of an ideal&nbsp;monatomic gas undergoes an adiabatic expansion in which its volume becomes eight times its initial value. If the initial temperature of the gas is <math> <mrow> <mn>100</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>K</mtext></mrow> </math> and the universal gas constant <math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mi>&#160;J</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>mo</mn><msup><mrow><mn>l</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mn>&#160;K</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, then how much is the&nbsp;decrease in its internal energy (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>) ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "900",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>V</mi></math><br /><br />For adiabatic process <math><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5/</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></math> for monoatomic gas<math><mo>}</mo></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>T</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>&#8901;</mo><msubsup> <mi>V</mi> <mn>1</mn> <mrow> <mi>&#947;</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </msubsup> <mo>=</mo><msub> <mi>T</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>&#8901;</mo><msubsup> <mi>V</mi> <mn>2</mn> <mrow> <mi>&#947;</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </msubsup> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>V</mi></mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math><br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>K</mn></math><br /><br />Loss in internal energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>900</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
